Speech to Text: Real-time Multilingual Transcription

A web app where you speak into your microphone and see the text appear in real time. It is built for mixed Hindi + English speech. Transcripts can be saved to a PostgreSQL database and managed (view, search, edit, delete) from a dashboard.

Live demo:   https://speech-recognition-beryl.vercel.app/
Backend API: https://speech-recognition-t5pu.onrender.com
Repository:  https://github.com/MayankArya123/speech-recognition


Features
Real-time speech-to-text with interim (live) and finalized text
Hindi + English (mixed) and English (India) recognition modes
Auto-restart when the browser ends a recognition session after a pause
Save transcripts to PostgreSQL with a custom title
Dashboard with transcription history and full CRUD (create, read, update, delete)
Toast notifications for success, loading, and error states
Tech Stack
Layer	Technology
Frontend	React (Create React App), Tailwind CSS, lucide-react, react-hot-toast, Axios
Speech recognition	Browser Web Speech API (SpeechRecognition)
Backend	Node.js, Express
ORM	Prisma
Database	PostgreSQL (Supabase)
